This was a long, hard session. The cycle-2 fix itself was small — 8 lines added, 6 removed in one Java populator. The path to get there was wasteful. リドワンさん was right to be frustrated throughout, and every correction landed a structural improvement on the way out.

The core failure was straightforward in retrospect: when リドワンさん said *"Let's start with 262233"*, I treated it as casual debugging phrasing. The Quest workflow has explicit triggers for this exact pattern — they're documented in `quest/quest-protocol.md`, they're reinforced by `ticket-gate.js` as a UserPromptSubmit hook. None of them fired because (a) the prose form had been compressed during the 2026-05-22 decomposition and (b) `ticket-gate.js` regex required a `QA/FAT/UAT` prefix that リドワンさん's natural phrasing didn't have. Five cycle-1 test apps with verified pengguna logins were sitting in `1. Notes.txt` from 2026-05-20. I burned multiple SQL roundtrips re-discovering `PTMLK/01/L/PRZ/2026/20 + nor.aini@melaka.gov.my` when it was literally entry #5 in that file. The full BA journal in `0. Brief/History.txt` (77 lines, 6 entries spanning cycle 1 verification + cycle 2 reopen) I only tail-glanced.

The diagnosis when it finally came was clean: `populateJTRingkasanRisalatPRZ`'s filter relies on `rjk_agensi.mklmt_tmbhn` JSON containing `ADUN` or `DUN` keys to strip YB rows from the Jabatan Teknikal table. On FAT, the agensi UNIT PERANCANG EKONOMI NEGERI (id=13) carries `{"DUN":"Ayer Keroh","NAMA_YB":"YB TUAN KERK CHEE YEE"}` — descriptive metadata about a representative YB associated with the unit, NOT a classification that the unit IS a YB. The filter misinterpreted descriptive metadata as classification. The fix swaps the metadata-driven filter for a name-pattern filter (`YB`/`YB.` prefix OR `AHLI DEWAN UNDANGAN` substring) — convention humans actually follow when naming agensis. Verified against all 35 UAT `rjk_agensi` rows + the 3 FAT agensis on BA's app: catches all 6 real YBs, keeps all real JTs including UPEN. Commit `5023fbf2fc` on `mlk/qa/262233v2`, pushed to origin earlier in the session.

